Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:01:39 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 115/115] Meridian: Today's order by drag and drop; the
 Workbench stays overnight and its closed sessions leave Mission Control; the
 agent's tab glows

- A Today tab dropped on another goes right above or below it, also in the
  tab strip, so a restart keeps the order (MoveTodayTab).
- The auto-archive skips the Workbench tab: its agent sessions run on.
- A Workbench page that goes away (its tab closed) tells Mission Control its
  sessions stopped, as Stop does; they no longer show as running.
- Claude Code can be started with --resume (its list of the project's
  recent sessions).
- The agent's tab id (a tab handle) is matched to the sidebar's NodeIds
  ("<handle>:<type>"): the page card and the sidebar row glow again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
